# Committed wasmtime reading for realloc-wait.wasm — a cabi_realloc that calls waitable-set.wait (#990).
# Built:       wasm-tools parse realloc-wait.wat -o realloc-wait.wasm   (wasm-tools 1.258.0)
# Engine:      wasmtime 49.0.2 (3c8a3e79a 2026-10-02), -W component-model-threading=y -W component-model-async=y
# Box:         darwin/arm64 (Apple Silicon).
#
# Invocation:  --invoke 'arg("hi")'
# Output:      wasm trap: cannot leave component instance      (backtrace: allocmod, the realloc)
# Exit:        nonzero
#
# Invocation:  --invoke 'res()'
# Output:      wasm trap: cannot leave component instance      (backtrace: allocmod <- cm, the child's task.return)
# Exit:        nonzero
#
# Invocation:  --invoke 'ctl("hi")'
# Output:      2
# Exit:        0
#
# Meaning:     a realloc runs with may_leave = False (definitions.py LiftLowerContext.reallocate), so the
#              checked built-in waitable-set.wait traps whether the realloc lowers an argument (arg) or a
#              cross-component result (res), and the unchecked context.set does not (ctl).
# Burroughs:   all three match (TestAReallocThatCallsABuiltInTraps), and res traps on the may_leave reason.
#              Until 2026-10-18 this line said res returns 0 because a late store's error had no reader (#994).
#              That stopped being true at #1034: its F0 runs this child's store inside the lower, because the
#              child resolves in its first segment. A store that does run late is realloc-wait-late.wasm.
